-- | The closed set of administrative roles for the AccessControl layer.
--
-- Using a sum type (rather than free `Text`, as in EVM's `bytes32` role ids)
-- keeps role identifiers exhaustive, typo-proof, and lintable — see
-- docs/ADMIN-LAYER-PLAN.md §1 (correction C4). New roles are added here as the
-- registry grows; every consumer that pattern-matches on `Role` is then forced
-- by the compiler to handle the new case.
module SimpleToken.Admin.Roles where

-- | A single administrative capability a registry administrator can grant.
--
-- `Admin` is the root governance role — the OpenZeppelin `DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE` /
-- `Ownable` owner analogue. A holder of an `Admin` capability may issue and
-- revoke other (non-`Admin`) capabilities (delegated governance), which is how
-- operational "ownership" is handed to a new party without reassigning the
-- immutable instrument admin party. See docs/ADMIN-LAYER-PLAN.md §5.
--
-- Enforcement status (what currently gates on each role):
--   * `Pauser` — enforced by `Rules_SetPaused`.
--   * `Admin`  — enforced by the `TokenAdministrator` delegated choices.
--   * `Minter` / `Burner` / `BatchProcessor` — RESERVED: defined so capabilities
--     are mintable ahead of the slices that consume them (AL-5/6 mint/burn,
--     V2-10 delegated settlement). No choice gates on them yet, so granting one
--     authorizes nothing today. Do not treat them as live access control until
--     their slice lands.
data Role
  = Minter          -- ^ (reserved) May create holdings out of band — future mint slice (AL-5).
  | Burner          -- ^ (reserved) May archive holdings out of band — future burn slice (AL-6).
  | Pauser          -- ^ May flip the registry pause flag (see SimpleToken.Rules). Enforced.
  | BatchProcessor  -- ^ (reserved) Delegated SettlementFactory_SettleBatch — future slice (V2-10).
  | Admin           -- ^ Root governance: may issue/revoke capabilities (owner analogue). Enforced.
  deriving (Eq, Show)

-- | Single source of truth for the delegation policy: whether a holder of an
-- `Admin` capability (a governance delegate) may issue or revoke this role.
--
-- The genesis root may manage every role; delegates may manage only roles for
-- which this returns `True`. This caps the governance hierarchy at one level —
--   root → Admin delegates → delegable operational roles —
-- and is used by BOTH the delegated-issue and delegated-revoke paths so the
-- policy cannot drift between them (see SimpleToken.Admin.Authority).
--
--   * `Admin` is root-only: no re-delegation, no delegate-vs-delegate or
--     delegate-vs-root governance changes.
--   * Reserved roles are root-only until their enforcing slice lands, so a
--     delegate cannot pre-mint one and retroactively gain power when that slice
--     starts gating on it. A reserved role graduates by flipping its case to
--     `True` in the same change that adds its enforcement.
--
-- The explicit per-constructor cases are deliberate: adding a new `Role` forces
-- a deliberate delegation decision here (non-exhaustive-match warning).
delegableRole : Role -> Bool
delegableRole Pauser = True
delegableRole Admin = False
delegableRole Minter = False          -- reserved (AL-5)
delegableRole Burner = False          -- reserved (AL-6)
delegableRole BatchProcessor = False  -- reserved (V2-10)
